From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: do not duplicate RADV's pipeline cache

The per-game Vulkan pipeline cache is kept for every pipeline compiled during
one session. Flushing it serializes the growing cache but does not release its
entries. On the PS5 the renderer is RADV, so keeping Eden's cache alongside the
driver cache duplicates that lifetime across area changes. The existing helper
already disables the Eden cache for the proprietary NVIDIA and AMD drivers;
RADV belongs to the same class for this purpose.

The regular Eden graphics/compute pipeline maps remain unchanged and still
provide the per-game cache and eviction policy. This only prevents the second
VkPipelineCache from retaining compile state on RADV.

Confirm on the console with identical warm area-change runs: the RADV driver id
must be present, `vulkan_pipelines.bin` must no longer be loaded/written, and
`EDEN_POOL_LEDGER`/`EDEN_MEMORY` should show a higher largest free block without
an increasing pipeline-cache contribution. If the target reports a different
driver id, this patch is intentionally a no-op and that log is required before
changing the predicate.

---
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -431,6 +431,7 @@ bool DriverCachesPipelines(const Device& device) {
     switch (device.GetDriverID()) {
     case VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY:
     case VK_DRIVER_ID_AMD_PROPRIETARY:
+    case VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_RADV:
         return true;
     default:
         return false;
     }
